  "identifier": "gow-ragnarok-chapter-builds-2026",
  "headline": "God of War Ragnarok chapter builds: skill priorities and gear set plans across the main story",
  "description": "A phase-based build timeline for The Path (18 missions): what to prioritize in skills (weapons, shield, companion) and which gear-set roles to assemble as you progress.",
  "articleBody": "Goal: remove decision friction per story point. Instead of chasing one \"best\" item, this page fixes roles (stability, burst, exploration) and provides representative sets you can assemble around the time they become available.\n\n0. Universal skill priorities (good in every chapter)\n- Shield: invest into your chosen defense style (parry or evade) to build a stable base\n- Leviathan: improve reliable single-target control (freeze/frost uptime)\n- Blades: crowd control first (pull, AoE, burn) to reduce incoming damage\n- Spear: safe ranged confirms and detonation patterns for guaranteed damage\n- Companion: stagger/status tools that create healing and punish windows\n\n1. Phase A (Missions 1–4): fundamentals\nMissions: 1 Surviving Fimbulwinter, 2 The Quest for Tyr, 3 Old Friends, 4 Groa’s Secret\n- Skills:\n  - Shield: commit to parry-first or evade-first and strengthen it\n  - Blades: add short, fast AoE options for trash fights\n  - Axe: prioritize low-commitment, consistent hits\n- Gear roles:\n  - Stability (recommended): defense/sustain leaning + short runics\n  - Exploration: cooldown leaning for more frequent runic windows\n- Route notes: secure shops and shortcuts, upgrade when level gaps show\n\n2. Phase B (Missions 5–8): establish a midgame set around Vanaheim\nMissions: 5 The Lost Sanctuary, 6 The Reckoning, 7 The Runaway, 8 Into the Fire\n- Skills:\n  - Blades: your main crowd-control engine\n  - Shield: handle guard-break style pressure with safer responses\n  - Companion: pick stagger/status arrows/spells first\n- Gear roles:\n  - Status build (example: Lunda-style): strong into midgame bosses\n  - Stability build: scales with difficulty\n- Route notes: once the River Delta is open, build one midgame foundation set\n\n3. Phase C (Missions 9–13): lock in your 3-weapon loop\nMissions: 9 The Word of Fate through 13 Creatures of Prophecy\n- Skills:\n  - Spear: throw + detonate as safe confirms\n  - Axe: freeze control for single targets\n  - Blades: AoE suppression, paired with companion control\n- Gear roles:\n  - Burst: cooldown/runic rotation to create more short damage windows\n  - Stability: reduce one-shot risk and recover from mistakes\n- Route notes: upgrade before you feel stuck; level gaps are real difficulty spikes\n\n4. Phase D (Missions 14–18): endgame tuning\nMissions: 14 Unlocking the Mask through 18 Beyond Ragnarok\n- Skills:\n  - Shield: create punish windows via counters\n  - Runics: prefer short, landable options over long animations\n  - Companion: plan a \"stop\" tool for boss specials\n- Gear roles:\n  - Endgame burst (example: Berserker pieces): high risk, high reward; consider partial use\n  - Ultra-stability (example: Steinbjorn-style): removes failure modes on high difficulty\n- Route notes: use mission 17 as a clean breakpoint if you want to assemble endgame sets pre-finale\n\n5. Minimal per-chapter template\nIf you are unsure in any chapter:\n1) keep weapon levels close\n2) run 2 short runics + 1 emergency relic\n3) companion for stagger/status\n4) learn only 3 consistent punish windows per boss\n\nA separate playbook page covers the cross-chapter checklist and detour timing in a step-by-step route.",
  "articleSection": "game-guide",
  "inLanguage": "es",
